<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <!-- ONE ENTITLEMENT, and the choice is measured rather than minimal-by-taste.

       `com.apple.application-identifier` = <TeamID>.<bundle id>. It is the claim
       that gives the helper its own keychain access group, and the value MUST
       equal the profile's own `com.apple.application-identifier`
       (`SHA2U6KT7V.com.local-operator.lopkeyagent`); the assembly script asserts
       that equality and fails the build otherwise.

       WHY NOT `keychain-access-groups` AS WELL. It is not needed — measured
       shapes (f) and (T) PASS with the application identifier alone — and it is
       actively worse to carry: with a keychain-access-group entitlement and a
       MISSING or stale profile the bundle is SIGKILLed by the kernel (measured
       shape Q, exit 137), whereas the same missing profile with the application
       identifier alone degrades to the fully diagnosable errSecMissingEntitlement
       (-34018, shape Q2). A smaller claim and a failure mode a user can read.

       WHY THIS FILE IS IN THE REPOSITORY WHILE THE PROFILE IS NOT. The
       entitlement has to name a real app id for codesign to accept it, and an app
       id is public: it appears in the signature of every wheel we publish, and
       `codesign -d` prints it from any installed helper. Two hyphens in a row are
       illegal inside an XML comment, which is why this sentence does not name
       codesign's flag verbatim. The
       PROFILE is different — it carries the Developer ID certificate, is bound to
       this team, and must be refreshable when it or the certificate is rotated, so
       it travels as the `MACOS_SIGNING_PROFILE_BASE64` secret and is written into
       Contents/embedded.provisionprofile by the build. Committing it would put one
       team's identity into every fork's build; committing this string only means a
       fork edits it (and Info.plist, and its profile) together. -->
  <key>com.apple.application-identifier</key>
  <string>SHA2U6KT7V.com.local-operator.lopkeyagent</string>
</dict>
</plist>
